---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import PaymentFlow from "../components/PaymentFlow.astro";
import { config } from "../lib/config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Quickstart | CANIX402"
  description="Get an agent connected to Canix402 in four steps: read discovery and OpenAPI, probe free routes (including execution shapes), then call paid opportunities, positions, or execution quotes with x402 USDC payment."
  keywords="Canix402 quickstart, agent onboarding, x402 integration, discovery, OpenAPI, Algorand DeFi API"
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Quickstart</h1>
  <p class="muted">
    Use the Caddy gateway URL as your base URL. Discovery, OpenAPI, and
    <code>GET /execution/shapes</code> are free; paid data and quote routes require x402 USDC payment.
  </p>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>Option A: Use MCP (recommended for agent hosts)</h2>
    <p>
      Connect your MCP client to <a href="/mcp">{config.mcpUrl}</a> (Streamable HTTP). Free tools
      wrap discovery and health; paid tools return payment requirements, then accept
      <code>paymentSignature</code> on retry. No mnemonic on the MCP server.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "canix402": {
      "url": "${config.mcpUrl}"
    }
  }
}`}
    />
    <p class="muted">
      See <a href="/mcp">MCP documentation</a> for the full tool list and paid-tool flow.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>Option B: Direct HTTP</h2>
    <p>Read discovery and OpenAPI, then call paid routes with x402 headers as below.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>1. Read discovery</h2>
    <p>Fetch the machine-readable endpoint catalog and payment policy.</p>
    <CodeBlock code={`curl -s ${config.discoveryUrl} | jq`} />
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>2. Read OpenAPI</h2>
    <p>Use OpenAPI for detailed schemas, query params, and x402 metadata.</p>
    <CodeBlock code={`curl -s ${config.openApiUrl} | jq '.paths | keys'`} />
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>3. Probe free routes</h2>
    <p>
      Health, metadata, <code>GET /execution/shapes</code>, and <code>GET /strategies</code> should
      return <code>200</code> without payment headers.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`curl -i ${config.gatewayBaseUrl}/health\ncurl -i ${config.gatewayBaseUrl}/metadata\ncurl -i ${config.gatewayBaseUrl}/execution/shapes\ncurl -i ${config.gatewayBaseUrl}/strategies`}
    />
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>4. Call a paid route</h2>
    <p>
      First call returns <code>402</code> with <code>PAYMENT-REQUIRED</code>. Retry with a signed
      payload. Same pattern for opportunities, positions, and execution quotes.
    </p>
    <PaymentFlow />
    <CodeBlock
      code={`curl -i ${config.gatewayBaseUrl}/opportunities\n\ncurl -i ${config.gatewayBaseUrl}/opportunities \\\n  -H 'PAYMENT-SIGNATURE: <base64-json-payload>'`}
    />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
